SANS NewsBites
Volume 28, Number 71

TOP STORY:
Vulnerability: CVE-2023-46604
Vendor: Apache Software Foundation
Product: Apache ActiveMQ
Affected Versions: 5.18.0 through 5.18.2, 5.17.0 through 5.17.5
Vulnerability Type: Remote Code Execution
Attack Vector: NETWORK
MITRE ATT&CK Technique: T1190 (Exploit Public-Facing Application)
Exploitation Status: ACTIVE_IN_THE_WILD
Attack Outcome: EXPLOITATION_REPORTED
Affected Sector: Financial Services, Manufacturing, Healthcare
Publication Date: 2026-09-14

DETAILS:
Ransomware operators are actively weaponizing CVE-2023-46604 in Apache ActiveMQ to gain initial access to enterprise infrastructure. The vulnerability enables an unauthenticated attacker with network access to execute arbitrary shell commands by manipulating serialized class types in the OpenWire protocol.

MITIGATION:
Upgrade to Apache ActiveMQ 5.18.3, 5.17.6, or newer versions immediately. Restrict OpenWire broker port (61616) to trusted internal subnets.

Confidence: 0.91
